(1) There is a utility class called called CreateTestFile, found in:

  ../src/main/scala/net/shrine/ontology/indexer/CreateTestFile.scala

  This class can be used to re-generate "resources/act_ontology_subset.txt", using as
  inputs "resources/category_definition.txt" and a complete ontology file such as "ACT_ontology_covid19.txt"
  (way too large to be committed, ask someone on the team for a copy)

  Its output is on Git and should be updated when CreateTestFile is run based on a new ontology
  and/or category definition


(2) Running LuceneIndexerTest

  LuceneIndexerTest.testCreateIndex() relies on the following two files:

  resources/act_ontology_subset.txt
  resources/category_definition_with_unicode_characters.txt

  These files are committed to the resources folder.


(3) The LuceneIndexer class is at:

  ../src/main/scala/net/shrine/ontology/indexer/LuceneIndexer.scala

  which also uses "resources/act_ontology_subset.txt" and "ACT_ontology_covid19.txt" and
  generates a lucene_index.zip file.


NOTES:

  category_definition_with_unicode_characters.txt and category_definition.txt must be kept in sync manually.
  The only difference should be extra unicode characters in category_definition_with_unicode_characters.txt, to
  match the unicode characters added by CreateTestFile



